                <pb facs="0238" n="152" sameAs="frus:frus1927v01/pg152"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15 a 1/539b: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chairman of the American Delegation</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gibson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-08-03T14:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 3,
                                1927—2 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>95. This morning the Democratic leader in the Senate (Robinson) called on me. I
                    discussed with him the entire situation at Geneva. Thoroughly approving our
                    course, he says he will support it. If speeches are made, he said we should
                    state our position fully and frankly.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
